Description: Draw windows from another GPU through a CPU copy
 On Intel+NVIDIA hybrid laptops, NVIDIA composites a monitor wired to its
 own ports. Windows drawn by GL/Vulkan clients (on either GPU) showed
 stripes of wrong content there, all the time, while wl_shm windows were
 fine. When a client dma-buf has to be drawn on a GPU other than the one
 that imported it, read it back once through the importing GPU and upload
 it like a wl_shm buffer. MIR_CROSS_GPU_CPU_COPY=0 restores direct import.
 .
 Copy buffers are pooled and reused once nothing holds them, so a window
 redrawing on the other GPU's monitor doesn't zero and fault in a new
 multi-megabyte buffer (and allocate a new texture) per frame. While
 $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/umoja-debug-windows exists, the amount copied is logged
 every 10 s with the most-copied buffer sizes.
Author: Umoja
Forwarded: no

